Here is a quote from an email I received:

>From the original sender: "please see the attached invoice."

The line above was escaped with a leading '>' by the mbox writer because it began with
"From " - per mbox quoting, a reader must not treat it as the start of a new message. This
fixture is a single message; if a reader mis-parses the quoted line as a boundary it will
report two messages instead of one, or discard the rest of this message's body.
